1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,823
Allowance is agentic wallet infrastructure on Solana.

2
00:00:03,873 --> 00:00:08,344
Every AI agent gets its own wallet key, with rules the chain enforces.

3
00:00:09,644 --> 00:00:12,255
Handing an agent your private key is risky,

4
00:00:12,305 --> 00:00:14,731
and a server-side guard can be bypassed.

5
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:18,258
Allowance puts the rules inside a Solana program instead.

6
00:00:19,558 --> 00:00:20,770
It has four layers.

7
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:23,095
A vault only you can withdraw from.

8
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:27,013
A session key for each agent, with its own caps and expiry.

9
00:00:27,063 --> 00:00:30,600
An MCP server, so Claude or Cursor can use the wallet.

10
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,788
And agent_pay, which checks every rule on-chain.

11
00:00:35,088 --> 00:00:37,065
Ask Claude to pay your friend.

12
00:00:37,115 --> 00:00:38,889
It calls the transfer tool,

13
00:00:38,939 --> 00:00:42,402
the MCP server signs agent_pay with the agent's key,

14
00:00:42,452 --> 00:00:45,442
and the program decides. A yes moves USDC.

15
00:00:45,492 --> 00:00:48,550
A no fails on-chain, with the rule that fired.

16
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:54,311
In the dashboard you issue an agent a session: 0.05 USDC per payment,

17
00:00:54,361 --> 00:00:56,503
2 USDC a day, named contacts,

18
00:00:56,553 --> 00:00:59,145
and a reputation floor for everyone else.

19
00:00:59,195 --> 00:01:01,272
Sign with Phantom, and it's live.

20
00:01:02,572 --> 00:01:05,798
The dashboard has a page for each part of the wallet:

21
00:01:05,848 --> 00:01:09,877
the vault and its kill switch, agent sessions, contacts, activity,

22
00:01:09,927 --> 00:01:11,360
approvals and merchants.

23
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:14,018
Everything is read straight from the chain.

24
00:01:15,318 --> 00:01:18,302
Then just ask. Over the cap? The chain refuses,

25
00:01:18,352 --> 00:01:20,884
and Claude tells you exactly which rule.

26
00:01:22,184 --> 00:01:26,741
Every payment and every refusal is on-chain, with the agent's reason.

27
00:01:26,791 --> 00:01:30,414
Refusals show in gold, with the rule that stopped them.

28
00:01:31,714 --> 00:01:34,014
Need more than the cap? The agent asks,

29
00:01:34,064 --> 00:01:37,930
and you approve that one payment with a single Phantom signature.

30
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:40,280
One switch freezes every agent at once.

31
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:46,373
It's built with Rust and Anchor, a Model Context Protocol server,

32
00:01:46,422 --> 00:01:49,204
x402 payments and a Next.js dashboard,

33
00:01:49,254 --> 00:01:52,258
and it's covered by thirty LiteSVM tests.

34
00:01:53,558 --> 00:01:58,099
Allowance. Wallets for AI agents, with rules the chain enforces.

35
00:01:58,149 --> 00:02:00,108
Live on Solana devnet today.
